# The kitty keyboard protocol's flag 4, report alternate keys: the base layout
# key, the key's character on the US PC-101 layout. Under flags 5 (1 and 4),
# Ctrl+С on a Russian layout sends the base layout key 99, c, after an empty
# shifted key; with Shift held the shifted key С, 1057, comes first. A key
# whose base layout key is its own code sends none.
# spec: kitty's Comprehensive keyboard handling in terminals: Report alternate keys; ADR-1005 D2, D9 and D13 slice 3
# capability: key-kitty-base-layout-key
size 20 2
needs key-forms
send "\e[>5u\e[?u"
check
reply "\e[?5u"
cmd key;sym=6d3;ascii=63;unicode=441;unshifted=6d3;base=63;mods=4
cmd key;sym=6f3;ascii=43;unicode=421;unshifted=6d3;base=63;mods=5
cmd key;sym=61;ascii=61;unicode=61;unshifted=61;base=61;mods=4
check
reply "\e[1089::99;5u\e[1089:1057:99;6u\e[97;5u"
